Hashmap class implements the map interface. It make use of hashing techniques to store, access, search and delete the element
in O(1) time complexity. Basically we store the data in the form of key value pair in hashmap using put method.

when we insert the data in the form of key value pair, the key will be undergoing the hashing and a hashcode will be generated.
This hashcode is used in resolving the index in bucket array where the data is to be mapped. After resolving the index, hashmap
stores the key value pair in the bucket, prior to that hashmap checks whether the key is already present in the bucket, if it is
present the value is updated. Sometimes different keys generate same hashcode and these goes to the same bucket this condition is 
said to be hash collision. This Hash collision can be resolved using Linked lIst.

HashMap make use of LinkedList, if there is any hash collision. If there is huge hash collisions, then the linked list size may
increases to a extent where the lookup becomes worst approximately O(n).

So in order to boost the look up, hashmap replaces the linked list with tree which is called treeification. So that the lookup time
reduces to o(log n).

In the retreieval process, we retrieve the value using get method and by passing key into it. The key again undergoes the hashinh
hashcode generates, bucket index will be resolving and hashmap fetches the values from the specific bucket if present if not it returns null.

We make use of put method itself for the updation also, if the key already exists the value will be updated and the old value
is returned if no key is already present then it adds to the buck and return null value.



